      "faqs": [
        {
          "id": 145380,
          "title": "What is MUBI FEST London?",
          "body": "MUBI FEST is a three-day festival of films, talks, music and activities, all designed for film lovers, at East London’s Hackney Picturehouse. Arrive early or stay after your screening to experience all of the festival, including an arcade of interactive activities, the MUBI Library, free shorts programmes, and great food and drinks.\n\nThe festival is presented by **MUBI**, the production company, film distributor and streaming platform focused on elevating great cinema.",
          "order": 0
        },
        {
          "id": 145381,
          "title": "What kind of films are shown?",
          "body": "A mixture of previews of MUBI Releases, including some of the first UK screenings of *Rose, Minotaur, Coward* and *A Long Winter* – plus exciting recent releases and iconic cinema classics.\n\nPlease note many of our films are restricted to 18+ and this event is not designed for families.",
          "order": 1
        },
        {
          "id": 145382,
          "title": "Will there be food and drinks at the festival?",
          "body": "Of course! You can get drinks, snacks and popcorn at the Hackney Picturehouse bar, and resident chefs from Original Flava will be cooking up Caribbean food all weekend.",
          "order": 2
        },
        {
          "id": 145383,
          "title": "Who can attend?",
          "body": "MUBI FEST London is open to all people over the age of 18. You don’t need to work in the film industry or to know a lot about film – just have a curiosity about great cinema from around the world.",
          "order": 3
        },
        {
          "id": 145384,
          "title": "How and when can I book tickets?",
          "body": "Tickets are only available exclusively through DICE – no tickets will be sold at the venue in advance or on the day.\n\nFinal tickets will be released at 10am on Tuesday, October 27.",
          "order": 4
        },
        {
          "id": 145385,
          "title": "Can I choose where to sit?",
          "body": "Seats are unreserved, so please arrive at the advertised start time to nab your favourite spot and to sit with friends.",
          "order": 5
        },
        {
          "id": 145386,
          "title": "Is Hackney Picturehouse wheelchair accessible?",
          "body": "Yes, all the screens and spaces where MUBI FEST London will take place at Hackney Picturehouse are fully accessible to customers with limited mobility. There are also multiple accessible toilets.\n\n**Wheelchair Space tickets are available to purchase. If you're in need of a companion ticket, please send a request to DICE and we will assist you.**\n\nView more information about Hackney Picturehouse’s accessibility here: https://www.picturehouses.com/cinema/hackney-picturehouse/accessibility",
          "order": 6
        },
        {
          "id": 145387,
          "title": "When should I arrive at my screening?",
          "body": "There will not be any trailers before screenings so we recommend getting to the cinema early to explore the event, and being seated at the advertised time.",
          "order": 7
        }
      ],
